4. **`apps/web/src/in-app-links.test.ts`** (new). Copy the file walk from `apps/web/src/writing.test.ts`, which already uses `import ts from "typescript"`. Write exactly this:
   ```ts
   // #2562: every link to a screen of the app moves in place. An `<a>` in a non-test `.tsx` under
   // `apps/web/src` whose `href` is a `paths.` entry or an address starting with `/` carries
   // `onClick={followInApp(…)}` (`routes/nav.tsx`), which moves without a page load and leaves a
   // modified or middle click to the browser, or opens a new tab (`target="_blank"`). A bare one reloads
   // the site: the read cache, the engine's WebAssembly and the audio unlock go with it. An `href` passed
   // in a variable (`action.to`) is its caller's to pair; FULL_LOADS lists the links that load the page on purpose.

   import { readdirSync, readFileSync, statSync } from "node:fs";
   import { dirname, join, relative } from "node:path";
   import { fileURLToPath } from "node:url";

   import ts from "typescript";
   import { describe, expect, it } from "vitest";

   const SRC = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));

   /** Every non-test `.tsx` under `dir`, `test/` directories aside, as writing.test.ts walks them. */
   function sources(dir: string): string[] {
     return readdirSync(dir).flatMap((name) => {
       const path = join(dir, name);
       if (statSync(path).isDirectory()) return name === "test" ? [] : sources(path);
       return name.endsWith(".tsx") && !name.endsWith(".test.tsx") ? [path] : [];
     });
   }

   /** One `<a` opening tag. */
   type Anchor = {
     /** Its file, relative to `apps/web/src`. */
     file: string;
     /** `file:line` of its `<a`. */
     at: string;
     /** Its `data-testid` as written (`shellTestid.loadFailedHome`), "" without one. */
     testid: string;
     /** Its `href` is a `paths.` entry or an address starting with `/`. */
     internal: boolean;
     /** Its `onClick` calls `followInApp`. */
     follows: boolean;
     /** It opens a new tab (`target="_blank"`). */
     newTab: boolean;
     /** Where its `onClick` attribute starts and ends in the file's text, null without one. */
     onClick: { start: number; end: number } | null;
   };

   /** An `href` inside the app: `paths.…`, or a string or template starting with `/` or with `${paths.…}`. */
   const INTERNAL_HREF = /^(?:paths\.|\/|["'`]\/|`\$\{\s*paths\.)/u;

   /** An attribute's value as written: a string's text, a `{…}` expression's source, "" for none. */
   function valueOf(attribute: ts.JsxAttribute | undefined, source: ts.SourceFile): string {
     const value = attribute?.initializer;
     if (value === undefined) return "";
     if (ts.isStringLiteral(value)) return value.text;
     if (ts.isJsxExpression(value)) return value.expression?.getText(source) ?? "";
     return value.getText(source);
   }

   /** Every `<a` opening tag in one file's text, however many lines it spans. */
   function anchorsIn(file: string, text: string): Anchor[] {
     const source = ts.createSourceFile(file, text, ts.ScriptTarget.Latest, true, ts.ScriptKind.TSX);
     const out: Anchor[] = [];
     const visit = (node: ts.Node): void => {
       if ((ts.isJsxOpeningElement(node) || ts.isJsxSelfClosingElement(node)) && node.tagName.getText(source) === "a") {
         const attributes = new Map<string, ts.JsxAttribute>();
         for (const property of node.attributes.properties) {
           if (ts.isJsxAttribute(property)) attributes.set(property.name.getText(source), property);
         }
         const onClick = attributes.get("onClick");
         const line = source.getLineAndCharacterOfPosition(node.getStart(source)).line + 1;
         out.push({
           file,
           at: `${file}:${String(line)}`,
           testid: valueOf(attributes.get("data-testid"), source),
           internal: INTERNAL_HREF.test(valueOf(attributes.get("href"), source)),
           follows: valueOf(onClick, source).includes("followInApp("),
           newTab: valueOf(attributes.get("target"), source) === "_blank",
           onClick: onClick === undefined ? null : { start: onClick.getStart(source), end: onClick.getEnd() },
         });
       }
       ts.forEachChild(node, visit);
     };
     visit(source);
     return out;
   }

   /** The internal links that load the page on purpose, each with its reason. */
   const FULL_LOADS: readonly { file: string; testid: string; why: string }[] = [
     {
       file: "main.tsx",
       testid: "shellTestid.loadFailedHome",
       why: "a screen's code failed to load: Home is a real page load, so it fetches the current build (RouteErrorBoundary)",
     },
     {
       file: "routes/landing.tsx",
       testid: "landingTestid.hotseat",
       why: "the dev-only hotseat boots from a full page load's query",
     },
   ];

   function exempt(anchor: Anchor): boolean {
     return FULL_LOADS.some(({ file, testid }) => anchor.file === file && anchor.testid === testid);
   }

   /** Where an internal link would reload the site. */
   function strays(anchors: readonly Anchor[]): string[] {
     return anchors.filter((anchor) => anchor.internal && !anchor.follows && !anchor.newTab && !exempt(anchor)).map((anchor) => anchor.at);
   }

   const TREE = sources(SRC).map((path) => ({ file: relative(SRC, path), text: readFileSync(path, "utf8") }));
   const TEXTS = new Map(TREE.map(({ file, text }) => [file, text] as const));
   const ANCHORS: readonly Anchor[] = TREE.flatMap(({ file, text }) => anchorsIn(file, text));
   ```
   Then one `describe("#2562 every link to a screen of the app moves in place", () => { … })` holding the four tests listed under **Tests**.

5. **`apps/web/src/routes/almanac.test.tsx`**, the test at line 354. Keep its title's start and append, so it reads: `"R654 R661 the almanac's detail view renders the compact statistics block, names no source, and links the full stats page, in place on a plain click and left to the browser on a ctrl or meta click"`. Replace its last assertion (lines 412–415) with:
   ```ts
       const link = within(screen.getByTestId(INSPECT_DETAIL)).getByRole("link", { name: /view full stats/i });
       const fullStats = `/stats?tab=cards&card=${encodeURIComponent(unit.id)}`;
       expect(link).toHaveAttribute("href", fullStats);
       expect(paths.statsCard(unit.id)).toBe(fullStats);
       // #2562: a ctrl or meta click is the browser's; a plain one moves in place, with no page load.
       const here = `${window.location.pathname}${window.location.search}`;
       expect(here).not.toBe(fullStats);
       expect(fireEvent.click(link, { button: 0, ctrlKey: true })).toBe(true);
       expect(fireEvent.click(link, { button: 0, metaKey: true })).toBe(true);
       expect(`${window.location.pathname}${window.location.search}`).toBe(here);
       expect(fireEvent.click(link, { button: 0 })).toBe(false);
       expect(`${window.location.pathname}${window.location.search}`).toBe(fullStats);
   ```
   `fireEvent`, `within` and `paths` are already imported. Copy the pattern from `apps/web/src/economy/JlorePill.test.tsx:91`.

6. **`apps/web/src/routes/practice.test.tsx`.**
   - At the end of `it("one refused saved deck is sent to Decks in the singular, and the legal one stays selectable", …)`, after its `"Fix it in Decks to play it here."` assertion, add:
     ```ts
         // #2562: the Decks link moves in place on a plain click and leaves a ctrl or meta click to the browser.
         const decks = within(screen.getByTestId(T.deckHint)).getByRole("link", { name: "Decks" });
         const here = window.location.pathname;
         expect(fireEvent.click(decks, { button: 0, ctrlKey: true })).toBe(true);
         expect(fireEvent.click(decks, { button: 0, metaKey: true })).toBe(true);
         expect(window.location.pathname).toBe(here);
         expect(fireEvent.click(decks, { button: 0 })).toBe(false);
         expect(window.location.pathname).toBe("/decks");
     ```
   - At the end of `it("an active account that never saved a deck is sent to Decks, not to sign in", …)`, after its `toHaveAttribute("href", "/decks")` line, add:
     ```ts
         // #2562: in place, without a page load.
         expect(fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole("link", { name: "Decks" }), { button: 0 })).toBe(false);
         expect(window.location.pathname).toBe("/decks");
     ```

7. **`apps/web/README.md`.** Add a new paragraph right after the one beginning "A move between two menus cross-fades (R2117000)":

   > An `<a>` to a screen of the app (`href={paths.…}` or an address starting with `/`) carries `onClick={followInApp(…)}` (`routes/nav.tsx`), which moves in place and leaves a modified or middle click to the browser, or opens a new tab (`target="_blank"`); a bare one reloads the site, emptying the read cache and reloading the engine. `src/in-app-links.test.ts` holds it, with the links that load the page on purpose (`FULL_LOADS`) and why.

8. **Manual check of the guard, then restore it.**
   - Delete ` onClick={followInApp(paths.decks)}` from one Decks anchor in `PracticeSetup.tsx`.
   - Run the scan test. It must fail, naming `practice/PracticeSetup.tsx:<line>`.
   - Put the attribute back, and confirm with `git diff apps/web/src/practice/PracticeSetup.tsx` that only step 3's changes remain.

## Tests

`apps/web/src/in-app-links.test.ts`, inside the describe from step 4:
- `it("every internal link calls followInApp, opens a new tab or is a listed full load")`:
  - `expect(ANCHORS.filter((a) => a.internal && a.follows).length).toBeGreaterThan(50)` (59 after this change);
  - `expect(strays(ANCHORS)).toEqual([])`.
- `it("each listed full load is still there, an internal link that does not call followInApp")`: for each `{ file, testid, why }` in `FULL_LOADS`, take `found = ANCHORS.filter((a) => a.file === file && a.testid === testid)`, then:
  - `expect(found, why).toHaveLength(1)`;
  - `expect(found[0]?.internal, why).toBe(true)`;
  - `expect(found[0]?.follows, why).toBe(false)`.
- `it("taking the onClick off any one internal link that calls followInApp fails the scan at that link")`:
  - take `followed = ANCHORS.filter((a) => a.internal && a.follows && !a.newTab)` and expect `followed.length` to be greater than 50;
  - for each anchor in it:
    - read `text = TEXTS.get(anchor.file) ?? ""`;
    - throw `` new Error(`${anchor.at} calls followInApp with no onClick`) `` when `anchor.onClick === null`;
    - set `without = text.slice(0, click.start) + text.slice(click.end)`;
    - `expect(strays(anchorsIn(anchor.file, without)), anchor.at).toContain(anchor.at)`.
- `it("reads an opening tag across lines, and leaves an external link, a new tab and a variable href alone")`: join these lines with `"\n"`, then `expect(strays(anchorsIn("sample.tsx", sample))).toEqual(["sample.tsx:1", "sample.tsx:3", "sample.tsx:10"])`. Lines 1, 3 and 10 are the bare `paths.` link, the multi-line `"/terms"` link and the template link.
  ```ts
  const sample = [
    "const bare = <a href={paths.decks}>Decks</a>;",
    "const literal = (",
    "  <a",
    '    className="link"',
    '    href="/terms"',
    "  >",
    "    Terms",
    "  </a>",
    ");",
    "const template = <a href={`/stats?tab=cards`}>Stats</a>;",
    "const followed = <a href={paths.decks} onClick={followInApp(paths.decks)}>Decks</a>;",
    'const tab = <a href={paths.terms} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Terms</a>;',
    "const contact = <a href={CONTACT_URL}>Contact</a>;",
    'const away = <a href="https://example.com">Away</a>;',
    "const passed = <a href={action.to}>Go</a>;",
  ].join("\n");
  ```
  Do not put `${` inside a plain string.

The almanac and practice tests are the ones extended in steps 5 and 6.

Commands:
```
pnpm --dir apps/web test src/in-app-links.test.ts src/routes/almanac.test.tsx src/routes/practice.test.tsx src/stats/CardStatsBlock.test.tsx src/net/deploy-routes.test.ts src/net/cloudflare-config.test.ts src/writing.test.ts
pnpm --dir apps/web typecheck
pnpm exec eslint apps/web
```

## Done when

- [ ] `paths.statsCard` exists, and `CardStatsBlock` uses it as both the `href` and the `followInApp` target.
- [ ] A plain click on View full stats in the Almanac is prevented and lands on `/stats?tab=cards&card=<id>`. A ctrl or meta click is not prevented (almanac test).
- [ ] Both practice Decks links move in place (practice tests).
- [ ] The scan test passes on the tree, and its mutation test fails at every internal link whose `onClick` is removed. Step 8's manual check failed, and the file was restored.
- [ ] `CardStatsBlock.tsx` has no bare `20`.
- [ ] Every command under **Tests** is green.
- [ ] The harness checks are green: rustfmt, catalog, patches, rulings, clippy, cargo tests and web tests. Nothing here touches Rust or the wire, so a red check names a real problem.

## Risks

- **Import cycle.**
  - `CardStatsBlock` now imports `routes/nav.tsx`, and nav's graph already reaches `CardStatsBlock` (`FriendsButton → Skeleton → … → CardDetail`).
  - Cycles through nav exist already (`nav.tsx ↔ JlorePill.tsx`), and `followInApp` is a hoisted function used only at click time, so nothing reads it while modules load.
  - If any test reports an undefined `followInApp` or a module-load error, report it rather than restructuring nav.
- **Leaving the deck editor.** The detail is a portal owned by the route, so the route unmounts on the move, and so does the open dialog's back layer (R2127000; `go` moves over its history entry). A leave guard (R1754000) now holds the move where one is registered. A reload did not do that, and holding is the intended behavior.
- **Hidden information and rule 7.** Untouched: these links only navigate.
- **A wrong flag later.**
  - The scan judges only an `href` written as `paths.…` or as an address starting with `/`.
  - A link that must load the page goes into `FULL_LOADS` with its reason. Never loosen `INTERNAL_HREF` to make a flag go away.
  - Test 2 fails when an exemption goes stale.

## Open questions

None needs a person. These are the decisions the task left open:
- **Where `statsCard` goes in `paths`.** It goes after `stats`. The issue said "beside `almanacCard`", but the two stats entries belong together.
- **How the scan reads tags.** It uses the TypeScript AST, as `writing.test.ts` does, rather than a regex. An AST reads multi-line tags and the `=>` inside `onClick` arrows correctly.
- **The two extra links.** `main.tsx`'s load-failed Home and the landing page's dev hotseat link are deliberate full page loads (their comments say so). They are exempted with reasons rather than changed.
- **Variable hrefs.** An `href` passed in a variable (`action.to`, `way.href`) is not checked. The issue scoped the scan to `paths.…` and `/…` literals.
- **The README.** One sentence is added to `apps/web/README.md`, which is the app's contract, although the issue doesn't list the file.
